<!--
  A subsumption that only holds through nominals (reduced from fuzz seed 3208):

    C1 = {a2, a0}, C4 = {a4, a3}, C3 and C0 disjoint, C0(a0), C4(a0), C3(a4),
    T2 = not-C3 and C4 and not-{a1}

  a0 is in C4 = {a4, a3} and cannot be a4 (C0 and C3 are disjoint), so a0 = a3; an instance of
  T2 is in C4 but not in C3, hence a3 = a0, which is in C1: T2 is below C1.
  The model of T2 merges the test node with a3 = a0 and contains C1 only as part of the label of
  a0, without the internal consequences that C1 has in its own test. The pseudo-model pretest
  of the classifier compared the two models, found a consequence of C1 missing and dropped C1 as
  possible subsumer of T2 without a test, although the model of T2 contained C1 itself.
  Expected: the HermiT taxonomy in expected/nominal-merge-pseudo-model-classification.owl.xml.
-->
